    {
      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Former Ethereum Foundation Official Sues EF and Vitalik Buterin, Alleging Retaliatory Firing Over Mandate Dispute According to a complaint filed in the U.S. District Court for Colorado on November 4, former Ethereum Foundation Protocol Support lead Kayleen Fulton (Nixo) sued six defendants, including Ethereum Foundation entities and co-founder Vitalik Buterin, alleging retaliatory termination and disability discrimination. Fulton claims she was fired on April 6 after disclosing an ovarian cancer diagnosis and helping organize a letter signed by 53 employees opposing mandatory endorsement of the Ethereum Foundation Mandate. The complaint also cites a recorded conversation in which Buterin allegedly expressed concern that employees could influence organizational decisions by creating controversy. The allegations have not been established in court. — link",
      "category": "Ethereum & L2",
      "importance": 0.445,
      "age_hours": 24.0,
      "source_quality": "social",
      "evidence_status": "unconfirmed-social",
      "asset_scope": "asset-or-sector"
    },
    {
      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Largest U.S. Retail Brokerage Charles Schwab Adds Spot Trading for SOL, AVAX and LINK Charles Schwab, the largest U.S. retail brokerage, announced on November 9 that its Schwab Crypto platform has added spot trading for Solana (SOL), Avalanche (AVAX), and Chainlink (LINK), bringing its supported assets to five alongside BTC and ETH. The platform launched early access in May and opened to all eligible retail clients in October, charging a 0.75% trading fee. The service is currently available only to eligible customers in select U.S. states, excluding New York and Louisiana, and is not available outside the United States. — link",
      "category": "Altcoins & Projects",
      "importance": 0.445,
      "age_hours": 24.0,
      "source_quality": "social",
      "evidence_status": "unconfirmed-social",
      "asset_scope": "asset-or-sector"
    },
    {
      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Eighth-Largest U.S. Bank PNC Partners With Coinbase to Pilot USDC Payments for Corporate Clients PNC Bank and Coinbase announced an expanded partnership on November 9 to pilot USDC payment acceptance for corporate and institutional banking clients. Eligible participants can receive USDC payments, which are automatically converted 1:1 into U.S. dollars and deposited into designated PNC bank accounts. The service is powered by Coinbase Payment APIs and aims to improve payment efficiency, including for cross-border transactions. The pilot is initially limited to select clients. The two firms previously partnered to offer digital asset trading to eligible PNC Private Bank clients. — link",
      "category": "Institutional & Exchanges",
      "importance": 0.445,
      "age_hours": 24.0,
